\f1\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec3 \uc0\u55357 \u56536  Overview\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Terraform Cloud Agents
\f0\b0  let you run Terraform operations (like 
\f2\fs26 plan
\f0\fs24  and 
\f2\fs26 apply
\f0\fs24 ) inside your private network, rather than in HashiCorp's infrastructure. This is useful when:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Your infrastructure is inside a 
\f1\b private VPC
\f0\b0 , behind firewalls, or not publicly accessible.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 Terraform needs access to 
\f1\b internal APIs
\f0\b0 , databases, or private endpoints.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 You require 
\f1\b fine-grained control
\f0\b0  over the execution environment and networking.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 This guide will walk you through setting up a 
\f1\b Terraform Cloud Agent on AWS EC2
\f0\b0 , using 
\f1\b Docker
\f0\b0  to run the agent in a containerized environment.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

